				<wikidot:authorName>lavenderbloodstains</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2615908</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>god, i absolutely love stories like this. dramatic tensions and character building through the lens of an incredibly absurd and nonsensical world is <em>very</em> fun to read.</p> <p>i absolutely loved the characterization of Cowboy Hephaestus and the little hints at the bigger world around this story, the conceptual <strong>fire</strong> and the capitalization of certain terms such as Cowboy denoting that they were very different from the Earth's cowboy, etc.</p> <p>my personal favorite line in the story was &quot;Fish swim in schools, though Cowboy Hephaestus, and then, maybe, he died.&quot;</p> <p>+1</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
