					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12332607#post-4336329</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12332607/ooo-ooo-ooo-ooo-ooo-ooo-ooo#post-4336329</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 21 Aug 2019 06:59:07 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Zzuxon</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1496981</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p>Cowboy Hephaestus snapped back to the present, looking around him wildly. Damnit, Galileo had been expecting him. He’d set up Flashback Mines to trap him in yesterdays.</p> </blockquote> <p>Pure genius. Not just the idea of narrative devices like flashbacks being used as weapons to distract characters (though that is also pure genius) but the fact that the flashback in question was interesting, well written, had good worldbuilding and advanced the plot. It's presence in the narrative was justified by itself, but then this line puts an incredibly hilarious and insanely clever twist on the whole thing.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
